course: dictionary
lesson: 2750
title: When things go out of sight
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A disappearance is a noun for something that happens: someone or something goes out of sight or cannot be found any more. It is built from the word disappear, so if you know disappear, you can often guess what disappearance means.
explain: «all down, down, down, gradually—ruin and levelling and disappearance» The clue words are gradually and ruin. They show a slow loss, so disappearance here means things slowly vanishing under leaves and sand. Check it by swapping in vanishing: the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «animal-etiquette forbade any sort of comment on the sudden disappearance of one's friends» The clue word is sudden. The friends went quickly and unexpectedly, and nobody was allowed to mention it. A disappearance can be slow or sudden, so look for the clue word before the word itself.
fact: Disappearance is a noun: a disappearance, several disappearances.
fact: «Disappearance» means going out of sight, or not being found any more.
fact: «Disappearance» can also mean a species, a habit or a thing stopping existing, such as an animal dying out.
fact: Phrases you may meet are «a mysterious disappearance» and «since her disappearance».
fact: Clue words like «sudden» and «gradually» tell you how a disappearance happens.
exercise: In «the sudden disappearance of one's friends», what does disappearance mean? | Coming back home | A loud noise | A big party | *Going out of sight or being lost
exercise: Which word in «gradually—ruin and levelling and disappearance» tells you the change is slow? | stones | leaves | up | *gradually
exercise: Which phrase fits a mystery story about a missing cat? | a sunny picnic | *a mysterious disappearance | a quick snack | a happy birthday
test: Scientists write about the disappearance of a species. What does this mean? | A new animal is born | Animals sleep all winter | Animals run very fast | *An animal type stops existing
test: What kind of word is disappearance in «a disappearance»? | Adverb | *Noun | Verb | Adjective
exam: «The disappearance of the cat puzzled the whole street.» Which word shows the cat is no longer seen? | whole | street | puzzled | *disappearance
